      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving understandability.Now I have a clear picture of the test. I'll improve understandability by:\n1. Removing unused constants, helper methods, and imports (holdovers from a base class)\n2. Breaking the dense one-liner `assertThrows` chains into readable multi-step assertions\n3. Removing the dev annotation and commentThe improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes unused constants, dead helper methods, and unnecessary imports, then splits each dense `assertThrows` one-liner into two clearly labeled lines — one to capture the exception and one to assert its message — with inline comments explaining the intent of each scenario."
